    "q-148737": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148737",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=4\\sqrt[3]{x}-7.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=4\\sqrt[3]{x}-7\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=4\\sqrt[3]{y}-7.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4\\sqrt[3]{y}-7 \\\\ 4\\sqrt[3]{y} & =x+7 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{y} & =\\frac{1}{4}(x+7) \\\\ (\\sqrt[3]{y})^{3} & ={(\\frac{1}{4}(x+7))}^{3} \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{64}(x+7)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{64}(x+7)^{3}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
