    "q-148496": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148496",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt[3]{x-3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt[3]{x-3}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt[3]{y-3}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt[3]{y-3} \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{y-3} & =3x \\\\ {(\\sqrt[3]{y-3})}^{3} & ={(3x)}^{3} \\\\ y-3 & =27{x}^{3} \\\\ y & =27{x}^{3}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=27{x}^{3}+3.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
